###############################################################################
# Example Music Infrastructure - Git Line Ending Policy
###############################################################################

# Default behaviour
* text=auto

###############################################################################
# Linux / Unix files (always LF)
###############################################################################

*.sh          text eol=lf
*.bash        text eol=lf
*.zsh         text eol=lf
*.py          text eol=lf
*.pl          text eol=lf

*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf

*.cfg         text eol=lf
*.conf        text eol=lf
*.cnf         text eol=lf

*.ipxe        text eol=lf

*.service     text eol=lf
*.socket      text eol=lf
*.timer       text eol=lf
*.mount       text eol=lf
*.target      text eol=lf
*.path        text eol=lf
*.slice       text eol=lf
*.scope       text eol=lf
*.network     text eol=lf
*.netdev      text eol=lf
*.link        text eol=lf

*.rules       text eol=lf
*.env         text eol=lf

*.md          text eol=lf
*.txt         text eol=lf

###############################################################################
# Windows files (always CRLF)
###############################################################################

*.ps1         text eol=crlf
*.psm1        text eol=crlf
*.psd1        text eol=crlf

*.bat         text eol=crlf
*.cmd         text eol=crlf

*.reg         text eol=crlf
*.xaml        text eol=crlf
*.xml         text eol=crlf

*.inf         text eol=crlf
*.sif         text eol=crlf
*.unattend    text eol=crlf

###############################################################################
# Binary files (never modify line endings)
###############################################################################

*.png         binary
*.jpg         binary
*.jpeg        binary
*.gif         binary
*.bmp         binary
*.ico         binary
*.svg         binary

*.pdf         binary
*.zip         binary
*.7z          binary
*.gz          binary
*.xz          binary
*.bz2         binary
*.tar         binary
*.tgz         binary
*.iso         binary

*.exe         binary
*.dll         binary
*.msi         binary

*.woff        binary
*.woff2       binary
*.ttf         binary
*.otf         binary

###############################################################################
# bootstrap/web/ boot assets -- git-lfs (2026-07-27)
###############################################################################
# By directory, not extension -- kernel binaries here are routinely
# extensionless by convention (vmlinuz, linux-x86_64, wimboot, bsd.rd),
# so filename-based rules would miss most of what actually needs tracking.
# Populated either by bootstrap/setup-workstation-{linux,macos}.sh /
# bootstrap/Setup-Workstation.ps1 (benarbejde/asset_manifest.json's
# real-upstream entries -- Spejder, klargoring, wimboot, Debian, OpenBSD,
# gparted) or dropped in by hand -- Robert's own custom builds with no
# upstream (none currently in this repo -- Arch's airootfs was the one
# example, removed entirely 2026-07-27, see menu.ipxe's v2.10 changelog),
# or third-party vendor downloads not worth a manifest entry (3cx/, supplied
# directly by Robert 2026-07-27; its kernel turned out to be genuine
# unmodified Debian Bookworm and lives at debian/bookworm/x86_64/linux
# instead, see menu.ipxe's :3cx-install comment).
# Either way, once a file lands under these paths it goes through LFS, not a
# plain git blob -- keeps this repo's normal git history small regardless of
# source. Existing tracked files under bootstrap/web/debian/ predate this
# rule and were NOT retroactively migrated (that rewrites git history -- a
# separate, more invasive decision, not bundled into this one).
#
# rockylinux/ and arch/ deliberately NOT tracked here -- both removed entirely 2026-07-27
# (Robert's call, see menu.ipxe's v2.10 changelog entry), not deferred. Re-add rules for
# either only if a real, working asset comes back behind them.
#
# winpe/ is scoped to wimboot* ONLY, not the whole directory -- wimboot
# itself (github.com/ipxe/wimboot) is GPL2, no Microsoft code in it, fine to
# distribute. The actual WinPE .wim is NOT -- Robert confirmed 2026-07-27
# this repo cannot redistribute it (Microsoft ADK licensing). See
# .gitignore's matching exclusion for the hard technical guard against ever
# committing one by accident.
#
# 2026-08-31: spejder/, proxmox/klargoring/ and gparted/ REVERSED out of LFS
# tracking entirely -- Robert's call. Both spejder and klargoring have a
# real upstream home of their own (github.com/knightmare2600/{Spejder,
# klargoring} releases -- see benarbejde/asset_manifest.json), and gparted
# has the real upstream Live ISO (gparted.org) -- committing the built
# artefacts here too was pure duplication, and the single largest
# contributor to this repo blowing its LFS storage budget (2.54GB of the
# total pending backlog, confirmed 2026-08-31). All three stay wired into
# check_bootstrap_assets.py's Tier 2 + benarbejde/asset_manifest.json's
# fetch-on-demand path (bootstrap/setup-workstation-{linux,macos}.sh /
# Setup-Workstation.ps1) -- the harness flags them missing and fetchable,
# nobody has to remember to run anything by hand.
#
# bootstrap/web/debian/** removed the same day, same reasoning, but ONLY
# the 8 mini.iso-extracted kernel/initrd files (bookworm/trixie x
# x86_64/arm64) -- all fully wired in the manifest to Debian's own netboot
# mini.iso (fetch_archive()'s .iso/7z extraction path, checksum-verified
# against Debian's real SHA256SUMS, verified live 2026-08-13).
# late_command.sh and the two lvm-*.seed files stay plain git-tracked
# below -- they're Robert's own hand-authored files with no upstream
# source at all (late_command.sh is the preseed's post-install hook,
# referenced from docs/bootstrap/bootstrapping.md; the seeds are actively
# read by menu.ipxe's ${seed} variable), never covered by the manifest,
# and were wrongly swept up by an earlier too-broad whole-directory
# removal attempt this same day before being caught by check_doc_index.py
# / check_bootstrap_assets.py and redone precisely.
#
# History rewritten (git-filter-repo, exact paths only -- not the whole
# bootstrap/web/debian/ directory, which would have touched Initial Commit
# itself, since a placeholder debian/{arm64,x86_64}/ existed there before
# the 2026-07-27 bookworm/trixie split) to remove these -- nothing had
# reached origin yet, confirmed before rewriting, so this was safe to do
# locally rather than leaving dead weight in history forever.
bootstrap/web/openbsd/**             filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
bootstrap/web/winpe/**/wimboot*      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
bootstrap/web/3cx/**                 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
bootstrap/web/hdt/**                 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Not PXE/HTTP-served (not under bootstrap/web/) -- a downloaded vendor SDK tool for the Intel
# vPro AMT KVM procedure (docs/hardware/ExampleMusic_Intel_vPro_AMT_NUC_Procedure.md), run from an
# admin's own Windows machine, not fetched by any boot script. ~59.5MB, LFS regardless of its
# non-web location for the same reason as everything else in this section -- keep it out of normal
# git history.
bootstrap/amt-sdk/**                 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Robert's own file, dropped directly in bootstrap/ (not a subfolder like amt-sdk/) -- a Windows
# tool to assist migrating ESX to PVE, ~43.5MB. Filename-specific rule rather than moving it into
# a new subdirectory of its own -- not reorganising a file the way Robert placed it without asking.
bootstrap/starwindconverter.exe      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Salt Windows minion installers, dropped directly in bootstrap/web/windows/ (2026-08-10) -- the
# x86_64 one is an official Salt Project release (45MB), the arm64 one is Robert's own custom
# build tracking 3 still-unmerged upstream PRs (70MB, see docs/buildsheets/
# buildsheet-salt-minion.md and 82-salt-minion.yml). Pattern-scoped to these two files, not the
# whole windows/ directory -- that directory also holds scripts/unattend XML that should stay
# plain git-tracked text, not go through the LFS filter. Not retroactively migrated (same
# "prospective only, not a history rewrite" call already made for bootstrap/web/debian/ etc.
# above) -- these two files' own existing commits predate this rule; only re-committed here so
# they're LFS-backed going forward. Superseded 2026-08-10, same day -- see the
# bootstrap/web/windows/arm64|x86_64/** rule below, Robert restructured this into
# per-architecture subfolders (matching 50-binaries.yml's own files/{x86_64,arm64}/
# convention) instead of individual arch-suffixed filenames at the top level.
bootstrap/web/windows/Salt-Minion-Setup-*.msi filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Windows tool binaries by architecture, dropped directly in bootstrap/web/windows/
# {arm64,x86_64}/ (2026-08-10, Robert) -- ~281MB in arm64/ alone. Whole-directory rule,
# unlike the single-file Salt pattern above: every real file under either subfolder is a
# binary tool (Sysinternals, jq, VMware tools, WindowsTerminal, etc.), matching this
# section's own established "genuinely open source / freely redistributable, no
# manifest-driven fetch" precedent -- not a mix of scripts and binaries the way the
# windows/ directory itself is, so no narrower pattern is needed here.
# x86_64/ renamed to amd64/ same day (2026-08-11) -- this rule is now inert (nothing lives
# at x86_64/ any more) but left in place rather than deleted; the amd64/ folder itself isn't
# whole-directory LFS-tracked yet, on purpose -- see the single-file rule immediately below.
bootstrap/web/windows/arm64/**   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
bootstrap/web/windows/x86_64/**  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Salt x86_64 minion MSI only, at its new post-rename path (2026-08-11) -- single-file
# pattern, NOT a whole-directory bootstrap/web/windows/amd64/** rule like arm64's above.
# The rest of amd64/'s contents are still being reorganised by Robert and deliberately not
# committed/LFS-tracked yet -- only this one file, which 82-salt-minion.yml already depends
# on, needed fixing now. Broaden to a directory rule once amd64/ itself is ready to commit.
bootstrap/web/windows/amd64/Salt-Minion-3008.0-Py3-AMD64.msi filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
